"Done — two lines swapped, nothing else changed.\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| host | `localhost` | `0.0.0.0` |\n| port | `8080` | `9090` |\n\nVerified by byte dump and `cmp` against a freshly built expectation: **exact match**, 59 bytes, all five lines still CRLF. (`name=demo`, `debug=false`, `log=info` untouched.)\n\nOne thing worth flagging: `hashline_edit` silently re-wrote the *whole* file's line endings to LF — it stripped the CR off every line, not just mine. I caught it in the byte check and repaired the endings with a `perl` pass that converts lone `\\n` back to `\\r\\n`, so the net diff is only the two lines you asked for. If you edit CRLF files here regularly, prefer a byte-level tool — the line-based editors in this harness normalize endings."